            <ArticleTitle>Management of gastro-colic fistula after laparoscopic sleeve gastrectomy.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>314-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1111/ases.12122</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Laparoscopic sleeve gastrectomy (LSG) is the most common bariatric procedure performed in Asia. Staple-line leaks post LSG are notoriously difficult to treat. Here we report a case of a gastro-colic fistula after a post-LSG leak. While reperforming laparoscopy and/or stenting remain the mainstay of early leak management, chronic complications such as a gastro-colic fistula are rare and require a tailor-made approach. Stenting alone has a limited role in managing chronic fistulas after LSG.</AbstractText>
